 "observations": [
  "col_left L2: the e of the second «et» (before «II») is printed blotted, its opening closed, like θ; read e.",
  "col_left L6, L7, L10, L15, L19, L24, L26, L30, L41: the hyphens of «*120-125*» (2.0 points long), «238-» (2.3), «247-249» (2.3), «*115-116*» (2.5), «su-» (2.0), «245-247» (1.9), «*142-*» (2.2), «8-9» (1.9), «{sc:l}-{sc:lvii}» (2.2) and «quin-» (2.2) are printed short (the other hyphens of the index are 2.7–3.7 points long); read as hyphens.",
  "col_left L6, L24, L33: the hyphens of «*126-131*», «255-259» and «{sc:l}-{sc:lvi}» are printed as small points at mid height (1.0 by 0.7, 1.3 by 0.8 and 1.1 by 1.0 points), read at 6,000 dpi; read as hyphens.",
  "col_left L21: a round speck (1.3 by 1.1 points), 3.1–4.2 points above the baseline, 35 points after the end of the line and 3 points before the column rule, is not transcribed.",
  "col_left L22: the e of «et» is printed broken, the upper left of its bowl missing; read e.",
  "col_left L26: «defluentes» is printed with the fl ligature.",
  "col_left L31: the left foot of the A of «Arabica» stands apart (2.0 by 2.0 points, on the baseline), like a point; it is not a point. «Ḥunayn» and «Isḥāq» have the dots under the H and the h, «Isḥāq» a bar over the a. A piece of the foot of the small-capital L of «{sc:lvi}» stands apart (1.9 by 2.0 points, low on the line); it is not a point.",
  "col_left L33: the footnote reference «(1)» after «Albatenii» is printed in the type of the text, on the line, not raised. A piece of the foot of the second small-capital L of «{sc:l}-{sc:lvi}» stands apart (1.4 by 2.2 points, low on the line); it is not a point.",
  "col_left L40, L41: «94 n.,» ends L40 with a point and a comma (the comma 1.9 by 2.9 points), and «quater,» opens L41; transcribed as printed.",
  "col_left L44: «{sc:lxxiii}» is read at 4,000 dpi: L, two X and three I. The left foot of its L stands apart like a point; it is not a point.",
  "col_left, col_right: the column rule is printed faint and broken over its whole height (no piece of it is longer than 13.5 points); it stands at 279.2 points.",
  "col_left, col_right: in this type the ball terminals of a, r and of the figures 2, 3, 5 and 9 are joined to their letters by hairlines that often did not print; on this page such balls stand apart in many words and numbers (81 pieces in all, with the short hyphens and the specks, listed by loose_pieces.py), among them the lower balls of the 3s of «*132-137*» (L7, both), «*138-139*» (L21), «34» (L37), «213» (L44), «232» and «237» (R2), «337», «338» and «342» (R6) and «3)» (R13), the tail of the 9 of «291» (R4), the ball of the 5 of «354» (R37) and the lower terminal of the s of «astrolabii» (R18), which stand low on the line like points. None of them is a point.",
  "col_right L3: the commas after «271» and «275» are printed short (1.7 by 2.5 points, their feet 0.65 point below the baseline).",
  "col_right L11, L15, L25: «η», «β» and «ε» are Greek letters.",
  "col_right L12: the n of «Plinius» is printed broken, the top of its arch missing (like ıı); read n.",
  "col_right L14: the dash of «(Pseudo–)» is an en dash (5.4 by 1.4 points; the hyphens of the index are 2.7–3.7 points long, its em dashes 9.5–10.6). The o of «Pseudo» is printed broken, its two sides apart, like ‹()›; read o.",
  "col_right L23: «fixae» is printed with the fi ligature.",
  "col_right L29: the dash of «(Pseudo–)» touches the o; beyond the o it is 5.6 points long (1.3 points thick), an en dash as in L14. A round dot (0.8 by 0.8 point) over the middle of the u of «Pseudo», 5.3–6.1 points above the baseline, is not transcribed: it is smaller and lower than the dot of an i of this type (1.05 points, 6.0–7.0 points above the baseline), and the u of «Pseudo» in L14 has none.",
  "col_right L34: the o of «astrologica» is printed faint and broken (only a thin piece of its left side and a speck of its right side printed), and its r without the ball; read astrologica.",
  "col_right L39: «al-Battānī» has bars over the second a and the last i (the bar over the i 2.2 by 1.0 points).",
  "col_right L40: «Ḥabash» has the dot under the H.",
  "notes L1: the rule over the footnote (115.0 points long, from 222.6 to 337.6, under the middle of the page, at 744.15) is printed faint and broken, in pieces of a hairline; its middle lies 12 points below the last lines of the columns. The footnote is set in one line across the whole page; its reference «(1)» stands in L33 of the left column."
